Let $b_n = a_n - 1$. Then $b_n = (b_{n-1})^3$, and
\begin{align*}
a_0 a_1 a_2 \dotsm &= (1 + b_0)(1 + b_1)(1 + b_2) \dotsm \\
&= (1 + b_0)(1 + b_0^3)(1 + b_0^{9}) \dotsm.
\end{align*}
Using the formula for an infinite geometric series where $b_0 = a_0 - 1 = \frac{1}{3} - 1 = -\frac{2}{3}$, the product becomes:
\begin{align*}
a_0 a_1 a_2 \dotsm &= \frac{1}{1 - b_0} = \frac{1}{1 + \frac{2}{3}} \\
&= \frac{1}{\frac{5}{3}} = \frac{3}{5}.
\end{align*}
Thus, the product of the sequence is $\boxed{\frac{3}{5}}$.

